\section{Summary and conclusions}\label{sct::conclusion}
We analyzed the security of several widely used symmetric ciphers and hash functions against parallelized quantum advers

aries. We the security parameter, wall-time and physical footprint for each cryptographic primitive. Our attack model was on a brute force searching via a parallelized of algorithm, assuming a surface-code fault-ant architecture on defects and braiding.

It is worth that throughout we are assuming that bruteforce search where we treat the cryptographic a blackbox is essentially the optimal attack against SHA and AES, which is currently be.
